James inquired about the easiest method to copy tabular data from R to Excel without creating intermediate files like CSVs or Excel files. I suggested using the `clipr` package to copy data directly to the clipboard. I provided installation steps for `clipr` and a brief code example to illustrate how to use the `write_clip()` function to copy a data frame. This method allows for efficient data transfer from R to Excel by simply pasting the data directly into the desired location. I also mentioned a potential workaround for clipboard access issues on Mac users.
